    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d901">

                <pb facs="0981" n="969" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg969"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.5151/177: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-03-16T01:00:00+02:00">March 16, 1940—1
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:51 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>28. My telegram No. 19, March 5, 4 p.m., from Istanbul [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ankara</hi>]. Exchange Office there [Istanbul] advises that up to March 15
                    exchange permits issued since the resumption of exchange transfers on March 4
                    total $287,400. Transfers leave [<hi rendition="#italic">have?</hi>] now been
                    effected on all applications filed prior to July 1, 1939.</p>
                <p>Total unpaid applications for exchange transfer permits on file as of March 14
                    amount to $4,680,000.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
